00:05.640 --> 00:08.190
instead of just pick for each one,

00:08.190 --> 00:09.780
you can replace it with reword

00:09.780 --> 00:11.880
if you wanted to reword all of them.

00:11.880 --> 00:15.300
But what I wanna do next is focus on combining,

00:15.300 --> 00:16.950
let's do these two,

00:16.950 --> 00:18.450
where I have add bootstrap,

00:18.450 --> 00:22.320
and then whoops forgot to add bootstrap JavaScript script.

00:22.320 --> 00:24.480
So in this example, or in this commit,

00:24.480 --> 00:28.350
I added a CSS file for Bootstrap,

00:28.350 --> 00:30.090
and then in this next commit,

00:30.090 --> 00:33.810
I realized I had forgotten to add the JavaScript script.

00:33.810 --> 00:36.180
So two things that really both should be part

00:36.180 --> 00:38.010
of add bootstrap.

00:38.010 --> 00:39.600
So I want the contents of both commits.

00:39.600 --> 00:41.190
I don't wanna just delete this,

00:41.190 --> 00:42.630
but I wanna get rid of that message,

00:42.630 --> 00:44.850
I don't want to have a moment in history

00:44.850 --> 00:46.200
where you see this change.

00:46.200 --> 00:48.690
I want it to be incorporated in this commit.

00:48.690 --> 00:50.160
So we have an option to do that.

00:50.160 --> 00:52.890
We can use fixup, a different command,

00:52.890 --> 00:55.380
which basically says use the contents of this commit,

00:55.380 --> 00:58.410
but meld it or mush it into the previous commits,

00:58.410 --> 01:00.510
and get rid of its commit message.

01:00.510 --> 01:01.650
So that's what I want.

01:01.650 --> 01:04.260
I wanna just get rid of this commit message,

01:04.260 --> 01:05.640
take the contents of the commit,

01:05.640 --> 01:08.070
and mush it together with this one.

01:08.070 --> 01:09.450
So I'll show you that now,

01:09.450 --> 01:11.880
I need to figure out how far back I wanna rebase.

01:11.880 --> 01:13.410
I'll just do nine again,

01:13.410 --> 01:16.320
just we don't need to, but sure, nine.

01:16.320 --> 01:17.553
So it opens this up,

01:18.570 --> 01:22.440
and I need to find the one that I want to fix up.

01:22.440 --> 01:25.770
So it says, it's like squash, which will use the commit,

01:25.770 --> 01:27.900
but meld it into the previous commit.

01:27.900 --> 01:30.000
But this time, if we use fixup,

01:30.000 --> 01:32.760
it also discards the commit's log message.

01:32.760 --> 01:34.350
So squash does not do that,

01:34.350 --> 01:37.020
I tend not to use squash, I tend to use fixup,

01:37.020 --> 01:38.700
if I wanna combine commits,

01:38.700 --> 01:41.430
I probably wanna only keep one commit message,

01:41.430 --> 01:43.800
but keep the contents of both.

01:43.800 --> 01:46.260
Okay, so we'll start here,

01:46.260 --> 01:48.003
pick that, fine, keep it.

01:49.020 --> 01:51.900
